# Step 2.2 — registration (Flow 5). Run `bun run dev`; VS Code "REST Client" keeps cookies.
# Needs a hackathon (see hackathons.http) and a user with a complete profile (see profile in /api/me).
@base = http://localhost:3000
@origin = http://localhost:3000
@hackathon = hackfest-2026

### Sign in
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "email": "pat@example.com", "password": "REPLACE_ME" }

### My status before registering → registered: false (200, not 404)
GET {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/me

### Register → 201 (body must be {}; the JSON content type is required)
POST {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/register
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{}

### Again → 409 ALREADY_REGISTERED
POST {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/register
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{}

### My status after → registered: true, participantId, registeredAt
GET {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/me

### Detail now counts participants
GET {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}

### Unknown hackathon → 404 HACKATHON_NOT_FOUND
POST {{base}}/api/hackathons/no-such-hackathon/register
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{}

### A user without a GitHub username or skills → 409 PROFILE_INCOMPLETE, details.missing
# (sign in as that user first)
